# No auth config lives here on purpose. An entry like
#   //registry.npmjs.org/:_authToken=${NODE_AUTH_TOKEN}
# makes every plain `pnpm i` warn "Failed to replace env in config:
# ${NODE_AUTH_TOKEN}" for anyone without the variable set — publishing
# doesn't need it in the repo:
# - CI: actions/setup-node with registry-url writes the auth line to
#   ~/.npmrc and injects NODE_AUTH_TOKEN at publish time (see
#   .github/workflows/release.yml).
# - Local: put the auth line (with a real token) in your own ~/.npmrc.
# Generate a granular access token at
# https://www.npmjs.com/settings/agentiknet/tokens with "Bypass 2FA
# when publishing" enabled and scope @agentproto/*.
